{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they set out from the mountain of YHWH a journey of three days</b> – According to the plain sense, the cloud set out and traveled before them for three days, and the Ark traveled behind the cloud but ahead of the people, and it did not rest in any place until the third day at evening, when the cloud rested in the wilderness of Paran, and there was a good place for them to encamp. This is the meaning of \"to seek out a resting place for them.\" And when the cloud rested, they set up the Tabernacle and brought the Ark there, and it is not specified whether they also traveled at night."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:05.884161065Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}